      "id": "P52B-S1-LRPC-L-002",
      "q": "A matching reform lowers the natural unemployment rate from 6.4 percent to 5.6 percent. At the same time, an unexpected demand expansion lowers actual unemployment to 4.9 percent. Later inflation expectations fully adjust while the reform remains in place and no new surprises occur. Which decomposition separates the durable change from the initial cyclical change?",
